From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Shapes' display lists: polygons out of the view left out
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)

NNS_G3dGeSendDL sends a model's shape whole. With the 3DS port's geometry
engine on its own core, a list of 256 bytes or more goes through
NitroPort_Gx3dSendList first (after what's in the geometry buffer): its
triangles and quads in groups, a group wholly out of the view left out
on the game's side, before the geometry thread has to work its vertices
out (a map's shape spans the whole map; on Route 206's Cycling Road most
of it is off the screen). The scene is the same. It sends the list
itself and returns 1, or returns 0 and the list is sent as before.

---
diff --git a/libraries/g3d/src/gecom.c b/libraries/g3d/src/gecom.c
index b624632..3f6b94c 100644
--- a/libraries/g3d/src/gecom.c
+++ b/libraries/g3d/src/gecom.c
@@ -96,6 +96,23 @@ void NNS_G3dGeSendDL (const void * src, u32 szByte)
     NNS_G3D_NULL_ASSERT(src);
     NNS_G3D_ASSERT(szByte >= 4);
 
+#if defined(SDK_PORT_3DS)
+    /* (the 3DS port) A shape's display list, sent whole: its lists of
+     * vertices out of the view left out before the geometry thread sees
+     * them (NitroPort_Gx3dSendList), after what's in the buffer. */
+    if (szByte >= 256) {
+        extern int NitroPort_Gx3dSendList(const void *src, u32 bytes);
+
+        NNS_G3dGeFlushBuffer();
+        if (NNS_G3dFlagGXDmaAsync) {
+            NNS_G3dGeWaitSendDL();
+        }
+        if (NitroPort_Gx3dSendList(src, szByte)) {
+            return;
+        }
+    }
+#endif
+
     if (szByte < 256 || GX_DMAID == GX_DMA_NOT_USE) {
         NNS_G3dGeBufferOP_N(*(const u32 *)src,
                             (const u32 *)src + 1,
